From ec6f09b71a26cc9dfb30636e22b82157cfafec51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:06:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09284/11362] Enable seeded tool-loop repair on the scored path
 at the 0.6 gate

Operator decision, on the evidence from 4 seeded catastrophic cells: 2 convert
outright to recall 1.0 / accuracy 1.0 and flip the trust layer from reject to
accept, 2 return their seed unchanged. Recorded as a conversion rate rather
than a pooled mean, because the +0.44 arithmetic mean describes no cell in the
set. One conversion is verified out of sample (sb26, tail 1.0, scan clean); the
other has no scoreable tail because that window's single tail row IS the
excluded level-up row, which was checked against the instrument rather than
assumed. Memorisation scan clean on all four.

Turn cap 12 -> 8. Every win across both arms converged by turn 7. Seven runs
burned the 12-turn cap at 17-24 minutes each and none recovered, so 8 preserves
all 11 observed wins and cuts each cap-burner by a third.

SET IN THE KERNEL, NOT AS A CODE DEFAULT. The evidence is scored-path evidence.
The conductor runs orders of magnitude more inductions, where ~10 minutes and a
budget slot per miss is a different trade-off that nobody has measured. The code
default stays OFF and its tests still pin that, so this flip is one line to
revert and cannot leak into local or conductor runs.

Verified with the kernel's exact environment: repair active, cap 8, threshold
0.6, and the gate still refuses every case it should -- a trust-ACCEPTED engine
(`downstream_accepted_engine`), recall 0.93 (`recall_not_catastrophic`),
n_changing 2 (`insufficient_changing_evidence`), and an exhausted per-game
budget. Without the environment the defaults read OFF and cap 12. 64 tests green.

This is an engine-quality lever and not a levels lever. The induced goal
predicate has never fired on a real win state (0 of 31 across 49 evaluations),
so levels are won by exploration rather than by planning. Expect better engines.
Do not expect the score to move on this alone.

NOT YET IN A SUBMISSION: kernel v21 was prepped before this change and does not
contain it. Reaching the scored path needs a re-prep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
